### Healthcare Payment Gateway - merchant flow (Phase 2)
### Works with the IntelliJ HTTP Client and the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
### Start the stack first:
###   docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml --profile infra --profile core up -d
### Replace the {{...}} values from earlier responses (or use an http-client.env.json).

@gw = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Register a hospital (public). Response: merchant, apiKey {keyId, keySecret}, webhookSecret.
###    keySecret and webhookSecret are shown only in this response.
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/merchants
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: sample-register-001

{
  "legalName": "City Hospital Pvt Ltd",
  "displayName": "City Hospital",
  "contactEmail": "billing@cityhospital.example",
  "contactPhone": "+919800001234"
}

### Example response (201 Created, Cache-Control: no-store)
# {
#   "merchant": { "id": "01a1d131-fd8d-71c7-a2c4-14ddb1f6c853", "legalName": "City Hospital Pvt Ltd",
#                 "displayName": "City Hospital", "contactEmail": "billing@cityhospital.example",
#                 "contactPhone": "+919800001234", "status": "PENDING_ACTIVATION",
#                 "createdAt": "2026-11-12T19:17:56.91Z", "updatedAt": "2026-11-12T19:17:56.91Z" },
#   "apiKey": { "keyId": "hpgk_FgVWhMyHWD8bFdAzZ3cjVDAs", "keySecret": "<43 chars>",
#               "createdAt": "2026-11-12T19:17:56.95Z",
#               "notice": "Store keySecret securely now. It is not stored by HPG and cannot be shown again." },
#   "webhookSecret": "whsec_<43 chars>"
# }

### 2. Get an access token (OAuth2 client credentials, HTTP Basic = keyId:keySecret)
POST {{gw}}/oauth2/token
Authorization: Basic {{keyId}} {{keySecret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials

### Example response (200)
# { "access_token": "eyJraWQiOi...", "token_type": "Bearer", "expires_in": 899 }
# Decoded claims: { "sub": "hpgk_...", "mid": "<merchant id>", "roles": ["MERCHANT"],
#                   "iss": "http://merchant-service:8081", "exp": ... }

### 3. Read my profile
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/merchants/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Update display name / phone (PATCH: omitted fields unchanged)
PATCH {{gw}}/api/v1/merchants/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "displayName": "City Hospital - East Wing" }

### 5. Read payment configuration (defaults are applied at registration)
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/merchants/me/configuration
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Replace payment configuration
PUT {{gw}}/api/v1/merchants/me/configuration
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enabledMethods": ["UPI", "CARD", "NETBANKING"],
  "captureMode": "MANUAL",
  "minAmount": { "amount": "10.00", "currency": "INR" },
  "maxAmountPerTransaction": { "amount": "150000.00", "currency": "INR" },
  "dailyLimit": { "amount": "2000000.00", "currency": "INR" },
  "paymentTtlMinutes": 30,
  "maxAttempts": 3,
  "refundWindowDays": 90,
  "webhookUrl": "https://his.cityhospital.example/hpg/webhooks",
  "notifyPatientEmail": true,
  "notifyPatientSms": false
}

### Example error (422) when a limit exceeds the platform maximum
# {
#   "type": "https://docs.hpg.example/errors/limit-exceeds-platform-maximum",
#   "title": "Configured value exceeds the platform maximum", "status": 422,
#   "detail": "maxAmountPerTransaction exceeds the platform maximum of 500000.00 INR.",
#   "instance": "/api/v1/merchants/me/configuration",
#   "errorCode": "LIMIT_EXCEEDS_PLATFORM_MAXIMUM", "correlationId": "e28cf10a-...",
#   "timestamp": "2026-11-12T19:17:57.809Z",
#   "field": "maxAmountPerTransaction", "platformMaximum": { "amount": "500000.00", "currency": "INR" }
# }

### 7. Rotate the webhook signing secret (new secret returned once)
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/merchants/me/webhook-secret/rotate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. API key rotation: create a second key, switch clients to it, revoke the old one
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/merchants/me/api-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/merchants/me/api-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
DELETE {{gw}}/api/v1/merchants/me/api-keys/{{oldKeyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------- OPS (client "ops-console", secret = HPG_OPS_CLIENT_SECRET in deploy/env/.env) ----

### 9. Ops token
POST {{gw}}/oauth2/token
Authorization: Basic ops-console {{opsSecret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials

### 10. List merchants waiting for activation (sortable: createdAt, updatedAt, legalName, status)
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/admin/merchants?status=PENDING_ACTIVATION&page=0&size=20&sort=createdAt,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{opsToken}}

### 11. Activate
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/admin/merchants/{{merchantId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{opsToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "KYC documents verified" }

### 12. Suspend (new tokens are refused immediately)
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/admin/merchants/{{merchantId}}/suspend
Authorization: Bearer {{opsToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Chargeback investigation" }
